{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And it came to pass at the end.</b> Rashi explained: a term of end, as its Targum. And he needed to explain thus because we find מקץ meaning beginning, as it is written in Jeremiah: מקץ שבע שנים תשלחהו חפשי, regarding a Hebrew slave — and there it means the beginning of the seven years, for it is written in the Torah: six years he shall serve and no more. But מקץ שבע שנים תעשה שמטה — one cannot bring proof from there, for מקץ is needed there to say that the Sabbatical year releases only at its end, as explained above." "<b>And Pharaoh dreamed.</b> Not like the measure of the Holy One, blessed be He is the measure of flesh and blood: flesh and blood strike with a scalpel and heal with a bandage, but the Holy One, blessed be He, strikes with a scalpel and heals with a scalpel. Joseph was struck through the dream he dreamed about his brothers, and was healed through the dream of Pharaoh. And that is what the payytan composed: 'from the very blows He prepares the bandage.'"], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:06:49.447184127Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}